1.What is the specificity of an inline style?
A)100
B)500
C)1000
D)10000

✅ Correct Answer: C) 1000

Simple English:

An inline style is written directly inside an HTML element.

Example:

<p style="color: red;">Hello</p>

Inline styles have the highest specificity (except !important).

Specificity Values:
Element selector (p) = 1
Class selector (.box) = 10
ID selector (#header) = 100
✅ Inline style = 1000
Easy Remember:
Element = 1
Class = 10
ID = 100
Inline = 1000
Options:
❌ A) 100
❌ B) 500
✅ C) 1000
❌ D) 10000

✅ Final Answer: C) 1000


2.Which combinator selects the direct children of an element?
A)Space ( )
B)=+
C)>
D)~

✅ Correct Answer: C) >

Simple English:

The > (child combinator) selects only the direct children of an element.

Example:
div > p {
  color: blue;
}

This selects only <p> elements that are direct children of <div>.

HTML Example:
<div>
  <p>Selected ✅</p>
  <section>
    <p>Not Selected ❌</p>
  </section>
</div>

👉 Only the first <p> is selected because it is a direct child of <div>.

Easy Remember:
> = Direct child
Space ( ) = Any descendant (child, grandchild, etc.)
Options:
❌ A) Space ( ) → Selects all descendants
❌ B) =+ → Not a valid CSS combinator
✅ C) > → Direct child
❌ D) ~ → General sibling selector

✅ Final Answer: C) >


