7.Which pseudo-element inserts content after an element

A):after
B)::after
C):post
D)::end

✅ Correct Answer: B) ::after

Simple English:

The ::after pseudo-element adds content after an element.

Example:
p::after {
  content: " 😊";
}

Output:

Hello 😊

The 😊 is added after the paragraph text.

Easy Remember:
::before → Adds content before the element.
::after → Adds content after the element. ✅
Options:
❌ A) :after → Old CSS2 syntax (works in many browsers, but modern CSS uses ::after)
✅ B) ::after → Correct (modern syntax)
❌ C) :post → Not a CSS pseudo-element
❌ D) ::end → Not a CSS pseudo-element

✅ Final Answer: B) ::after
