10.Which selector styles highlighted text?
A)::mark
B)::selection  //answers
C)::highlight
d)::text


✅ Correct Answer: B) ::selection

Simple English:

The ::selection pseudo-element styles the text selected (highlighted) by the user.

Example:
::selection {
  background: yellow;
  color: black;
}

👉 When you select text with your mouse, the selected text will have a yellow background and black color.

Easy Remember:
::selection = Selected (highlighted) text ✅
Options:
❌ A) ::mark – Not a valid CSS pseudo-element
✅ B) ::selection – Correct
❌ C) ::highlight – Not the standard answer
❌ D) ::tex – Not a valid CSS pseudo-element

✅ Final Answer: B) ::selection
